C-LHarc for UNIX -- authors' terms
==================================

The source in this directory is C-LHarc for UNIX V1.00, the branch Kai Uwe
Rommel took from Yooichi Tagawa's V0.03a.  The version history at the head of
lharc.c is the authority on that lineage:

    /*  V0.00  Original                          1988.05.23  Y.Tagawa    */
    /*  V0.01  Alpha Version (for 4.2BSD)        1989.05.28  Y.Tagawa    */
    /*  V0.02  Alpha Version Rel.2               1989.05.29  Y.Tagawa    */
    /*  V0.03  Release #3  Beta Version          1989.07.02  Y.Tagawa    */
    /*  V0.03a Fix few bug                       1989.07.03  Y.Tagawa    */
    /*  V0.04  A lot of bugs fixed, strict mode  1990.01.13  Kai Uwe Rommel */
    /*  V1.00  f and t commands, v option added  1990.01.27  Kai Uwe Rommel */

Note that Tagawa's own line reached a DIFFERENT V1.00 (1989.09.22, continuing
to V1.01 on 1989.12.25).  Both statements below are reproduced because the two
V1.00s are not the same program: the first covers the V0.03 base this source is
built on, the second covers Tagawa's own V1.00.

The compression engine, lzhuf.c, credits the LZSS algorithm to Haruhiko Okumura
and the adaptive Huffman coding to Haruyasu Yoshizaki (1989.05.27).


Yooichi Tagawa's statement for V0.03, verbatim
----------------------------------------------

From `read.me' in the archive this source was taken from
(mwcbbs/lharc/lharc.tar.Z), under the heading "The text of the original
Read.me file follows":

                                    -*- Text -*-

    LHarc UNIX V0.03 Release #3  Beta Version

        This is FREEWARE.  But it's BETA-VERSION.

        Please reply to me.

        Sorry, lharc.doc file are written in JAPANESE (Shift-JIS KANJI)

                        Thank you.

                        Yooichi.Tagawa
                        Nikkei-MIX ID: y.tagawa


Yooichi Tagawa's statement for V1.00, verbatim
----------------------------------------------

From `READ.ME' in mwcbbs/386/lharc.zip, which carries Tagawa's V1.01 source:

                                    -*- Text -*-

    LHarc UNIX V1.00

        This is FREEWARE.

        Please send problems to me.

        Sorry, lharc.doc file are written in JAPANESE (Shift-JIS KANJI)

                            Thank you.

                        1989.09.19  Yooichi.Tagawa
                            Nikkei-MIX ID: y.tagawa


Copyright notice carried in the source
--------------------------------------

Every file in this directory carries:

        Copyright(C) MCMLXXXIX  Yooichi.Tagawa

Kai Uwe Rommel's V0.04 and V1.00 changes are recorded in the version history
above and are not accompanied by any statement of terms of their own.

What "FREEWARE" does and does not settle is unresolved; the word is the
author's, and it is stated without a list of conditions.
